# Development workflow

- Lifecycle: `docs/development-workflow.md`.
- Use a template from `docs/prompts/` for Cursor work; record the **approved prompt summary** in `docs/chat-workflow-log.md`.
- Inspect the repository before editing (`git status`, relevant files).
- Implement only the approved Cursor prompt scope.
- Stop and report when requirements conflict, migrations appear unapproved, or ownership is unclear.
- Use **Cursor Terminal** for git/pytest/Flask inside this repo; say the terminal name explicitly when documenting commands.
- Chat conversation titles in this Cursor/IDE workspace must always start with `BRAYMAN — <Topic>` to prevent cross-project context mixing with other workspaces (e.g. AiRIA).
- ChatGPT originating **ACTIVE CHAT TITLE** is separate traceability metadata. Begin CalibAi development responses with that exact title in bold; end with `END — <title>` after any Cursor prompt. Canonical: `docs/governance/continuity-and-anti-drift.md`.
- After implementation: report files changed, assumptions, risks, and exact test results for ChatGPT review before commit.
